{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user provided a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (Task ID: 5211) to add differential test cases to `cmd/ls/ls_test.go` for srd008-ls requirements R2.3 through R2.6. Specifically:\n   - R2.3: `-d` flag (list directories themselves, not their contents)\n   - R2.4: `-a` and `-A` flag precedence (last one wins)\n   - R2.5: `-t` flag (sort by modification time, newest first, name tiebreaker)\n   - R2.6: `-S` flag (sort by file size, largest first, name tiebreaker)\n   \n   The task requires adding DiffTest entries to the existing test slice, following the established differential testing pattern, and verifying tests pass with `go test ./cmd/ls/ -count=1`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: Go binary vs GNU reference binary (`gls`) via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - `testutils.DiffTest` struct with fields: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` to compile the Go binary\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gls\")` with `t.Skip` fallback for missing reference binary\n   - LC_ALL=C environment for deterministic locale-independent output\n   - Git is managed externally - NO git commands allowed\n   - Function size limit of 40 lines (hard limit from execution constitution)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd008-ls.yaml` (lines 1-200 read)\n     - Contains the SRD requirements. Key requirements for this task:\n     - R2.3 (line 98): `-d` must list directory entries themselves rather than their contents\n     - R2.4 (line 100): When both `-a` and `-A` are given, the last one on the command line takes precedence\n     - R2.5 (lines 102-103): `-t` must sort by modification time, newest